[Music]  new tonight another report of a stolen  car from a valet on the strip this comes  after we first shared the story of a  woman whose car went missing after  dropping it off victoria saha is live on  this story joining us live near the  paris hotel with a bit more victoria  brian for those of us who don't want to  use a self parking garage you might  think that using a valet is a better  option but now a woman says her car was  stolen from the paris hotel valet now  this is a second person reaching out to  us  with a busy city like las vegas hundreds  of thousands of people find their way  here many flying in but also many opting  to drive which means parking on the  strip but now we're learning it could  come with some risks last week we told  you the story about a woman whose range  rover was stolen from the valley at  paris hotel after someone found her  ticket then katie francis reached out  saying the same thing happened to her  months before when you saw our story  that we did a few weeks ago with a  similar situation what were your  thoughts  i was pissed because just to hear that  it's continuing to happen to people and  they're not doing anything francis used  the valet at the paris on march 23rd for  just an hour when she came out she  couldn't find her ticket so they're like  oh no problem your car's on the way up  you just need to fill out this paperwork  but while she was filling out her form  francis sees a woman get into her car  and drive away  you knew the ticket was gone we had  already filled out the paperwork  and yet you still just decided to have  this lady our keys francis says she was  told that woman handed them this valet  ticket and that is how she was able to  drive away with her car no questions  asked francis's car was missing for 10  days and when she got it back it was  trashed with multiple different license  plates found inside and she was told two  arrests were made  francis says the valley of paris didn't  give her any answers as to how this  happened so i called them and they said  they did practice standard protocol but  they don't require to check id when  returning a car to a customer the  manager at the valley of harris said  that they pride themselves in doing a  good job victoria zaha live local now

